# The OTHER direction, and it is a different fault: a `consumes` whose
# `acquires` is missing, so a correct program hands back what the count never
# saw arrive (M-marked-acquisition, panel 148 R2).
#
# **This case exists because it happened.** `examples/curl/main.hero` has
# carried `consumes` since panel 145 landed it on 2026-09-13, and the first
# counter built for this milestone killed that correct program at exit 134 with
# a message saying **`1 C handle(s) never given back`** — the exact opposite of
# what had occurred. One counter, two sentences: positive accuses the PROGRAM,
# negative accuses the BINDING, and the repair is one word on the producing
# declaration.
#
# The program below is right and its binding is not, which is the whole point:
# the diagnosis has to name the declaration, not the code.

extern "abort-handle-given-back-unmarked.h"
    record Slot tag Slot
    function slot_open(n: i64) -> Slot
    function slot_close(s: Slot consumes)
    function slot_value(s: Slot) -> i64

function main()
    a = slot_open(n: 7)
    print(slot_value(s: a))
    slot_close(a)
